#: ../fhir-harness/processes/content/ig-ast-cache.bpmn:113
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The AST is uploaded with the run, for that ref's own review; the shared cache is left alone."
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/processes/content/ig-ast-cache.bpmn:91
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The runner mounts the layers the IG repository's `index.lock.json` pins, then restores and judges the cache itself. When it is not valid (or `force` is set) it rebuilds with the Publisher fork (Tool `ig-ast-export`, `litlfred/fhir-ig-publisher` at the pinned `claude/ast-export` commit). A stale cache is first rebuilt incrementally (`IncrementalBuildCli`), falling back to a full `AstExportCli` build with `-tx`; a `force` run, a `pre-export` caller, or a missing or cannot-tell cache always builds in full, and a release needs a full build. The caller's optional `pre-export` overlay command runs before a full build; the inputs it changed are put back and the AST is recorded against the clean commit's input digest (`ig-ast.ts source-inputs`). The AST just built must itself be `valid` for the commit, or the run fails."
msgstr ""

